# Loops

A loop is one recurring responsibility that ends in a result outside your head. Read [docs/LOOPS.md](mdc:docs/LOOPS.md) before proposing, renaming, splitting or merging one, and [docs/VOICE.md](mdc:docs/VOICE.md) before writing any name.

## Every loop passes the six tests

Stranger, done, action, one-rule, everyone-has-one and ceiling. If it fails one, rewrite it, split it or drop it.

## Names

- A verb and an object, 8 words or fewer, in every language of the log.
- No names of people and no identifying details. "My partner," never her name.
- Name the output, not the decision behind it: "Get weeknight dinner on the table," not "Decide what's for dinner."
- Never start with: decide, choose, remember, remind, track, monitor, keep an eye on, stay on top of, think about, prepare, review, manage, handle. `validate()` enforces these by the log's protocol version: decide and choose fail from v1.1 (`naming.since` in [protocol.json](mdc:protocol.json)).

## Storage (`seed/loops.json`, D1 `loops` in the app)

```json
{
  "code": "R-PAR-01",
  "level": "still",
  "name": { "en": "Plan and book our date night", "es": "Planear y reservar nuestra cita" },
  "doneWhen": { "en": "The table is booked and on both calendars.", "es": "..." },
  "scope": { "en": "Covers our regular night out and anniversary plans. Birthday gifts and kid weekends are other loops.", "es": "..." },
  "estimate": { "howOften": "weekly", "hoursPerWeek": 1.5 },
  "triage": { "time": 2, "frequency": 3, "rules": 3, "digital": 4, "risk": 3, "source": "baseline" },
  "baseline": { "occurrences": 3, "confidence": "normal", "hoursPerWeek": 1.5, "approvedAt": "2026-03-30" },
  "evidence": "Calendar: recurring Friday events"
}
```

Optional: `scope` (public boundary: what counts and what doesn't), `measuring`, `over500`, `published` (R-PAR only), `visibility`, `changedCycle`, `retired`, `drops`.

## Rules enforced by `validate()` in [lib/protocol.mjs](mdc:lib/protocol.mjs)

- Codes are `BRANCH-AREA-NN` from protocol section 2.4 and are never reused. Retire a loop with `retired: true`, never delete it.
- A frozen inventory has exactly 100 active loops. Building mode allows 0 to 100.
- Ceilings (protocol 9.3): R-KID and P-HLT and C-PPL cap at assisted, R-PAR at delegated, P-FIN with `over500` at delegated.
- Levels are `still` (Still yours), `assisted` (Help me), `delegated` (Do it, I approve) and `autonomous` (Do it alone). `levelName()` gives the words people see; the keys never change.
- Measured is a mark, not a level: a loop is measured once its `baseline` is approved (`isMeasured()`). Logs from before v1.2 store `unmapped` and `mapped`; `upgradeLevels()` reads both as `still`.
- Above still needs an achieved stage at that level whose hold passed. Before v1.4 it also needs an approved `baseline`.
- Only unmeasured `still` loops can be `measuring`, 5 at most. Measuring is optional from v1.4.
- Levels change only through holds and drops, never by editing `level` directly.

## Private by default

`evidence` is never published. R-PAR loops stay hidden until `published: true`. `publicView()` is an allowlist: a new field is private until it is added there.

Run `npm test` after editing the seed. The tests validate the sample against every rule.
